S5 is an additive whole export mode. The existing `--write` and `--check`, their S3 `SOURCE_HEAD`, strict evaluator, R0 witness, and source guards remain intact. Use `node tools/rust-r1b/export-shared.mjs --s5 --write` and then `--s5 --check` only after the independent review pins below are frozen. Node 24.x, TypeScript 6.0.3, and Zod 4.6.1 remain mandatory.

The immutable R0 original still has 455 constants and 224 enum occurrences with normalized SHA-256 `3d126e07d5abf2c56f41c35fc25b78a13dbe094450b470e8bb4c950ce8a2986c`. No historical file is rewritten. The reviewed nominal identity file records original owner/schemaId/propertyPath and the 209 prior Rust family names; it supplies identities, never current wire values. Current values come from original TS interpreted by the old strict data evaluator and independently executed as the original closed TS/Zod module graph.

This S5 capture registers exactly index, shared-contracts, and rust-r4ghi-contracts.generated, including the canonical130 ExecutionAdmissionContextView addition. Semantic AST recognition covers 338 `z.enum` calls (214 legacy-module, 124 canonical-module), including line breaks before `.enum`; the earlier inspection-only319 observation missed those forms and is not current evidence. Computed Zod members, unknown factories/modules, hidden enums in helpers/callbacks, unknown data helpers and top-level constructs fail closed.

All 224 historical occurrences have explicit identities: 197 retain owner/property source, 27 migrate through actual module/named-provider ancestry. The source registry separately records 114 post-R0 occurrences, 446 unchanged historical constants and nine explicit replacements, 202 retained array nominal identities, 125 current inline families, and 16 canonical type bindings proven by exact TS imports/reexports. All 209 prior Rust nominal families survive. Equal wire lists never merge unrelated types. The original complete manifest renderer produces the neutral manifest, full Rust enums, and full generated tests.

Source commit A contains the reviewed OpenAPI file and `tools/openapi/checkpoints/r4ghi-s5/**` raw snapshots/provenance. S5 reads input-manifest02, requires all414 records and all declared snapshot paths to exist in A, and consumes the six exact snapshot sources (attributes, index, shared, canonical, auth entity, auth service) under their original logical paths. It reads OpenAPI and immutable R0 at their original committed A paths. Every consumed snapshot checks raw size/SHA and normalized SHA, and the A blob itself must match the consumed raw bytes via binary `git cat-file --batch`. The checkpoint directory/spec/R0 working, index and untracked guards all compare with fixed A. Live six logical files must exactly equal their raw snapshots before and after construction. No live dirty override or inferred HEAD is available.

Tool/identity/registration review belongs to separate commit B. The B files must be tracked and clean in the runtime checkout; independent exact generator and metadata hashes are also mandatory. `HEAD` is used only for B cleanliness and never assigned to A/sourceHead. Generated provenance distinguishes A's logical/physical raw input records from B's generator and registration identities.

Root execution sequence after independent review:

1. Commit approved A scope and verify its actual raw snapshot blobs. Do not include unrelated WIP Shared/Native products to make a source guard pass.
2. Apply the reviewed tool proposal and nominal/source registrations. Set registry `reviewStatus` to `Root-reviewed-S5-registration` and its `sourceHead` to the independently approved A hash. Set `review.mjs` sourceHead, final normalized registry/identity SHA, raw input-manifest02 SHA and the exact generator hash map. The map excludes review.mjs to avoid a self-referential hash; that file is still tracked/clean and included in output generator provenance. Any source/registry/tool change requires another review and updated exact pins.
3. Commit the independent B scope, then run the portable pure probes (`node tools/rust-r1b/s5/export-s5.probes.mjs`) and the real `--s5 --write`/`--s5 --check`. Inspect the three artifact diffs, run generated Rust tests and the actual crate check. Record B's actual commit/hash evidence separately from A.
4. Preserve old failed/partial inspection evidence. A candidate render, pure matcher fixture, or isolated generated-enum test is not a real Git-guard pass, whole-crate check, G3 or G4 certification.

The candidate leaves review pins null deliberately. It cannot write production outputs until Root freezes and commits the concrete reviewed A/B inputs. Pure author validation used the actual input-manifest02 raw SHA `3b9bea8727a4c89c1a8ad5c0a3891d0718d1435d4913c285dedebb4d524ec602`, generated 330 enums/1159 values, passed all43 pure probes, and compiled/tested the standalone generated-enum crate. The Root Git guards and real Root artifact write/check remain Root-run checks.
